  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. The project kicked off on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. Initially, the budget for phase one was set at $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and the integration of real-time analytics. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, including a prototype for secure file sharing, ahead of schedule. The executive board has since approved a total budget of $2 million to cover all research, development, and marketing phases. Additional budget allocations include $55,000 for a compliance plan (covering training and audits) and $15,000 for specialized training programs for the coding team and project managers. The team is also exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology. An onboarding session for the Zenith Innovations team was scheduled for April 15th, 2023, and a celebration for the testing milestone was held on October 10th."
